    {
      "id": 28612,
      "name": "broccoli",
      "username": "broccoli",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/broccoli/{size}/1861_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-04-22T16:21:42.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Hmm, then it sounds like they need a new keyword: “static”.  This would mean the damage is both irreducible and unincreasable.  Unfortunately, there’s no current way in the game to duplicate an amount of damage done without applying all the bonuses and penalties again <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/frowning.png?v=9\" title=\":frowning:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":frowning:\"></p>\n<p>That’s also why I assumed it just meant that it started the same.  I assumed the “equal amount of damage” meant only the initial damage.  If both hits start at 1 (or 2 if using Charge), and then you apply all the same bonuses and penalties to both hits, then, aside from damage reduction on the targets’ side, and Nemesis bonuses.  They would be equal.</p>",
      "post_number": 9,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:02:33.903Z",
